  "blurb": "Guillochon et al. (2010) run Ba as a whole binary: a 0.45 solar mass helium white dwarf donor at 0.915 of its Roche lobe and a 0.9 solar mass carbon-oxygen accretor, both settled in the Roche potential and tidally locked, in the frame turning with the orbit (tracking the pair, released after a merger). Each is threaded by its own tangled Kolmogorov field confined to the star (plasma beta 1e5 at the center, seeds 1 and 2). Helmholtz equation of state with he4, c12 and o16, watched for burning: once a step would release a tenth of a cell's internal energy the run stops and carries on with the 13 species of the aprox13 network, which burns. Lengths in units of 10,000 km. Start-up damping (velocities damped at rate 1, easing to zero by t = 10). Fill sweep below the onset, with refinement zones by tier around L1, the stream and the accretor: box 16 at 2048^3 with 5 levels, one orbit (t = 32).",
